      ],
      "correct": "4",
      "solution": "[IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/ca81259519cadfb2d5350673c220e419e60378e9770ad26512fc8e826a8d93f1.png] __Shortcut Trick__\n\nGiven equation: 12% of 980 − x% of 450 = 30% of 227\n\n⇒ 117.6 − 4.5x = 68.1\n\n⇒ 4.5x = 117.6 − 68.1 = 49.5\n\n⇒ x = 49.5 ÷ 4.5 = 11\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 11.**\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/c76c13ba2d2ab46b47f8a931ae621dac081a0cb266b142dc23f58659fac4a466.png] **__Alternate Method__**\n\n**Given:**\n\n(12% of 980) − (?% of 450) = (30% of 227)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nLet the unknown value be x.\n\n⇒ [12 ÷ 100 × 980] − [x ÷ 100 × 450] = [30 ÷ 100 × 227]\n\n⇒ [12 × 9.8] − [x × 4.5] = [3 × 22.7]\n\n⇒ 117.6 − 4.5x = 68.1\n\n⇒ 4.5x = 117.6 − 68.1\n\n⇒ 4.5x = 49.5\n\n⇒ x = 49.5 ÷ 4.5\n\n⇒ x = 495 ÷ 45\n\n⇒ x = 11\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 11.**\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f13e2ad6582c16aa62a83672e2547ad20a01fddb61962a1acce42eb9a1a99caa.png] **__Additional Information__**\n\nBODMAS Rule\n\nAlways follow the BODMAS rule (Brackets, Order/Of, Division, Multiplication, Addition, Subtraction) systematically to ensure mathematical accuracy in simplification.\n\nPercentage Shortcuts\n\nRemember that x% of y is exactly the same as y% of x. For example, 12% of 980 can also be solved as 98% of 120, which is logically equivalent and sometimes easier to compute.\n\nHandling Decimals in Division\n\nWhen dividing two numbers that have the same number of decimal places (e.g., 49.5 ÷ 4.5), simply ignore the decimal point and divide the whole numbers (495 ÷ 45) to quickly find the result.\n</p",
